26162	26346	25910	25910	him:--	1520	“ You know my genealogy , my good fellow ? I was the son of Lawyer Pepper , a shrewd old dog , but as hot as Calcutta ; and the grandson of Sexton Pepper , a great author , who wrote verses on tombstones , and kept a stall of religious tracts in Carlisle . My grandfather , the sexton , was the best temper of the family ; for all of us are a little inclined to be hot in the mouth . Well , my fine fellow , my father left me his blessing , and this devilish good head of hair . I lived for some years on my own resources . I found it a particularly inconvenient mode of life , and of late I have taken to live on the public . My father and grandfather did it before me , though in a different line . ' T is the pleasantest plan in the world . Follow my example , and your coat shall be as spruce as my own . Master Paul , your health ! ”
